  "description": "When exactly one movie clears the approval floor, RUNOFF is skipped entirely, so a stray veto row cannot disqualify the outright winner",
  "spec_clause": "State machine: 'RUNOFF - finalists computed. Veto screen, then pairwise. Skipped entirely when only one movie clears the approval floor.' + Phase 1: 'Exactly one clears it -> it wins outright, skip Phase 2.'",
  "rationale": "4 attendees, both movies have all 4 rows (coverage 1.00, attendee_votes 4) so both are eligible. m1: 3 yes -> approval 0.75 >= 0.50 -> clears. m2: 1 yes -> approval 0.25 -> does not clear. Exactly one movie clears the floor, so the round goes straight to DECIDED: m1 wins outright and the veto screen and pairwise step never happen. A Veto row from u2 on m1 exists in the input (a stale or client-side-bypassed write); because the veto step is not part of this round it must not be evaluated, must not disqualify m1 (which would leave zero options), and must not flip u2's standing vote. Expected veto_counts is empty because no veto tally is computed at all.",
